// An UNCALLED lambda whose body calls its function-typed parameter. `vl check` returns 0 (one
// unused-variable warning) and the emitter refuses with `emitProgram: function-value call arity
// has no interned signature` — clause 2. Nothing in the module interns an arity-1 closure
// functype, because a lambda binding does not mint one from its own signature and no call site
// mints one either.
//
// Four ingredients, each necessary: the LAMBDA spelling (`function apply(f: (i32) => i32): i32`
// runs), the parameter being CALLED in the body, the parameter's type being a FUNCTION type, and
// the lambda itself being UNCALLED. Any unrelated arity-1 call in the module, or an annotation on
// the binding, makes it run — which is the mechanism stated as a control. See D1474.
// Should print 7.
const apply = (f: (i32) => i32) => f(1)

print(7)
